@@ -0,0 +1,111 @@
+# ADR 0332: Mobile session controls over the local MCP control plane
+
+- Status: Proposed (implementation candidate; Desktop patch required; mobile E2E pending)
+- Date: 2026-10-19
+- Deciders: PI-Desktop maintainers
+- Related: [ADR 0203](0203-local-mcp-control-plane.md) ·
+  [ADR 0310](0310-local-permission-approvals-without-deadline.md) ·
+  [03-runtime/01-ipc-protocol](../spec/03-runtime/01-ipc-protocol.md) §13d ·
+  [03-runtime/03-tools-and-permissions](../spec/03-runtime/03-tools-and-permissions.md) §6–7 ·
+  [03-runtime/13-model-catalog-and-selection](../spec/03-runtime/13-model-catalog-and-selection.md) §4
+
+## Context
+
+The local MCP control plane already exposes project, session, Agent, and
+workspace operations. A paired mobile client can list and read Desktop
+sessions, create one, send a prompt, and stop it. Two useful controls were
+still missing:
+
+1. The client could read a session but could not choose a model when creating
+   it or switch an existing idle session without using the broad
+   `session/configure` operation. That operation also accepts mode, thinking
+   level, and `permissionMode`, including `auto`, so using it as a model switch
+   would risk changing unrelated policy.
+2. The Agent's pending AskTool questions and tool-permission requests were
+   available to the renderer, but not through the reviewed MCP catalog. A
+   remote client could therefore not see or answer the request that was
+   blocking the turn.
+
+The installed 0.20.1 build exposes neither a model-only switch nor the pending
+interaction read over this control plane. The `agent/pendingInteractive` IPC
+handler also returned the bridge's pending requests without proving that the
+requested id was a local desktop session or filtering the result by session.
+
+## Decision
+
+1. Add the dangerous `session/setModel` operation and named
+   `pi_session_set_model` tool. Its config contains exactly `providerId` and
+   `modelId`. It requires an existing local desktop session, an enabled
+   provider, a configured or cached model, and an idle session with no pending
+   Plan/Goal approval. It updates only the durable model binding; mode,
+   thinking level, permission mode, and title are preserved. Validation and
+   the write happen in the existing main-process and host-core paths.
+2. Add the read `agent/pendingInteractive` operation and named
+   `pi_agent_pending_interactive` tool. Native Pi sessions keep their own empty
+   path. Before returning anything for a desktop id, Electron Main verifies
+   that it names a local desktop session, then filters both the AskTool and
+   permission arrays to that session. Remote and unknown ids fail closed.
+3. Reuse the existing dangerous resolvers. `tool/resolvePermission` accepts the
+   local vocabulary, but a constrained remote client is expected to offer only
+   `allow-once` and `deny`. It must not expose `allow-session`, change
+   `permissionMode`, or answer Plan/Goal approvals or extension prompts
+   through this surface. `agent/askTool/resolve` accepts one
+   `string[] | null` entry per question; `null` is an explicit skip and answer
+   values are plain text.
+4. Keep capability discovery authoritative. A Desktop build without these
+   operation ids keeps the corresponding client controls unavailable; clients
+   do not fall back to `session/configure`, arbitrary IPC, or a fabricated
+   acknowledgement.
+5. Do not add a new persisted schema, a new transport, or a general-purpose
+   remote API. `session/setModel` is one host RPC in the existing session
+   domain; the pending read delegates to the existing Agent IPC handler.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- A paired client can choose a model at creation, switch an idle session's
+  model without changing its execution or permission policy, and resolve
+  ordinary tool and AskTool cards. Subscription, provider credentials,
+  secrets, and global settings remain outside the surface.
+- Remote approval is intentionally narrower than the desktop card. A remote
+  user cannot create a session-wide grant or move a session to Auto.
+- Reading pending state and resolving it are separate calls. A response is
+  authoritative only when the Desktop acknowledges it; a transport failure or
+  unknown result must be reconciled by re-reading and is never replayed
+  automatically.
+- The capability exists only with the additive Desktop patch based on
+  `589e5803a7a9f4ebf7ec1e8849c43e44b4a198f7` (v0.21.0-beta.4). An installed
+  0.20.1 build, or an unpatched build of that baseline, does not support it.
+  This ADR does not claim that an upstream release already ships it.
+- Plan/Goal approval, extension UI, attachments, thinking-level changes, and
+  permission-mode changes remain desktop-only.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+### Use `session/configure` for model switching
+
+Rejected: its accepted fields include permission mode and other session
+configuration. A client that intends only to change the model could silently
+alter policy, and the confirmation prompt would not describe the actual risk.
+
+### Expose `agent/pendingInteractive` without session scoping
+
+Rejected: the bridge can hold requests for multiple sessions, and the API must
+not let a caller read or infer another session's prompts. Native and remote
+sessions also have their own input paths.
+
+### Implement RACP for this client
+
+Rejected for this change: the local MCP plane already carries the same
+authorities and persistence, and RACP remains a separate remote-Host contract.
+Adding a second transport would duplicate authorization and lifecycle logic
+without serving the constrained mobile use case.
+
+## Verification
+
+Source-contract coverage is added in
+`apps/desktop/test/mcp-control.test.mjs`,
+`apps/desktop/test/pending-interactive-scope.test.mjs`, and
+`apps/desktop/test/session-model-only.test.mjs`, with host-core tests beside
+`session.setModel`. E2E-268 records the end-to-end desktop/mobile scenario.
+The documentation change that introduced this ADR did not execute those
+tests; the full Electron journey remains pending.
